WEBVTT

00:03.520 --> 00:04.820
Finished!

00:04.820 --> 00:06.180
Himeno's Garden

00:09.960 --> 00:11.620
The mini-garden is now complete!

00:12.820 --> 00:15.760
It's better outside, isn't it, Mom?

00:15.760 --> 00:17.350
How is it? Does it feel good?

00:24.400 --> 00:26.370
It's done, Mom.

00:27.210 --> 00:29.010
Will a pretty flower bloom now?

00:29.010 --> 00:31.740
A flower won't bloom just by planting it.

00:32.710 --> 00:35.810
It needs soil, water, and warm sunlight.

00:35.810 --> 00:39.010
If it's lacking any one of these things, it won't bloom.

00:40.220 --> 00:44.660
So you have to look after them well and protect them.

00:44.660 --> 00:48.020
Yeah, I understand! I'll protect the flowers!

00:52.930 --> 00:54.630
Protect?

00:57.300 --> 01:00.970
I get the feeling I'm the one being protected by everyone else.

01:01.510 --> 01:03.570
But nothing will get done by getting depressed!

01:07.410 --> 01:09.570
So, here's lots of water service!

01:12.420 --> 01:13.510
Oh, no!

01:13.950 --> 01:15.280
I'm sorry!

01:16.320 --> 01:17.520
Mayune!

01:18.160 --> 01:19.590
You wait right there!

01:22.780 --> 01:26.050
The boundless future stretches across the skies

01:22.780 --> 01:26.050
hateshinai mirai hirogaru kono sora

01:26.050 --> 01:30.090
And I am reborn anew

01:26.050 --> 01:30.090
atarashii jibun ni umare kawaru

01:30.090 --> 01:37.110
I'll make the snow of happiness fall all over the world

01:30.090 --> 01:37.110
sekaijuu shiawase no yuki o furasete miseru yo

01:41.160 --> 01:41.360
Prétear

01:49.340 --> 01:56.250
Destiny is there to be grasped, so stretch out your hands

01:49.340 --> 01:56.250
unmei wa tsukamu mono kono te jiyuu ni nobaseba ii

01:56.250 --> 02:01.040
There is no tomorrow which has already been decided

01:56.250 --> 02:01.040
kimerareta ashita wa nai

02:03.090 --> 02:09.990
Even if you say nothing, I know our meeting that day was no coincidence

02:03.090 --> 02:09.990
damatte ite mo wakaru ano hi deai wa guuzen janai

02:09.990 --> 02:14.900
I sensed eternity in your distant gaze

02:09.990 --> 02:14.900
tooi hitomi ni eien kanjita

02:16.730 --> 02:20.600
The light of the setting sun is beautiful

02:16.730 --> 02:20.600
kurete yuku yuuhi ga kirei

02:20.600 --> 02:23.740
If the cold wind glimmers

02:20.600 --> 02:23.740
tsumetai kaze ga hikareba

02:23.740 --> 02:29.510
I can hear your voice drifting gently

02:23.740 --> 02:29.510
anata no koe sotto kikoeteru

02:29.680 --> 02:29.980
Knowing that I'm not alone in my heart

02:29.680 --> 02:34.450
kokoro no naka hitori janai koto itai hodo

02:34.450 --> 02:36.990
Warms it so much that it hurts

02:34.450 --> 02:36.990
kono mune o atsuku suru

02:36.990 --> 02:39.720
It all begins from the point of believing

02:36.990 --> 02:39.720
hajimaru ne shinjiru koto kara

02:39.720 --> 02:43.390
These feelings are proof of being alive

02:39.720 --> 02:43.390
kono kimochi ikiru akashi

02:43.390 --> 02:43.690
The endless future and the expanding skies

02:43.390 --> 02:46.600
hateshinai mirai hirogaru kono sora

02:46.600 --> 02:50.630
Allow me to be reborn anew

02:46.600 --> 02:50.630
atarashii jibun ni umare kawaru

02:50.630 --> 02:56.740
I'll make the snow of happiness fall all over the world

02:50.630 --> 02:56.740
sekaijuu shiawase no yuki o furasete miseru yo

02:56.740 --> 03:01.340
Holding hands with you

02:56.740 --> 03:03.340
sono te tsunaide

03:03.600 --> 03:06.960
A Promise Made Under the Sunlight

03:09.300 --> 03:13.170
It's been a month since I started to use that hair growth formula.

03:13.670 --> 03:14.970
I wonder if it's stress?

03:18.910 --> 03:21.810
Good morning, Ma'am!

03:25.750 --> 03:26.820
Good morning...

03:26.820 --> 03:28.020
Ma'am!

03:28.020 --> 03:28.780
...Kaoru!

03:29.250 --> 03:30.960
Good morning, Natsue.

03:30.960 --> 03:32.860
My, where were you?

03:32.860 --> 03:35.290
I was taking a walk out in the yard.

03:35.290 --> 03:37.350
I wanted to go with you as well.

03:37.860 --> 03:39.850
It must be stress after all!

03:50.140 --> 03:51.970
Okay, no sign of Mayune anywhere.

03:58.350 --> 03:58.820
Awayuki Pharmaceuticals

04:00.620 --> 04:03.520
See you!

04:03.520 --> 04:05.260
Dad, what was that just now?

04:05.260 --> 04:06.830
Good morning, Himeno.

04:06.830 --> 04:09.890
Natsue said she had a board meeting at the pharmaceutical company.

04:09.890 --> 04:12.360
I see. What a flashy way to attend.

04:12.360 --> 04:13.420
This plaster...

04:14.400 --> 04:15.600
Where should I take it?

04:15.600 --> 04:16.430
Hayate?!

04:17.170 --> 04:19.700
What are you doing here?!

04:19.700 --> 04:21.710
Dad saw you!

04:21.710 --> 04:23.470
You know him, Himeno?

04:24.210 --> 04:26.910
This is Hayate, my new part-time helper.

04:26.910 --> 04:29.610
Part-time?! You hired him, Dad?!

04:29.610 --> 04:34.780
Yes, he was wandering around in our yard, and I did want some help, so...

04:35.320 --> 04:37.860
What kind of reason is that to hire someone?!

04:37.860 --> 04:38.890
Not to mention the fact...

04:38.890 --> 04:41.150
What I do is none of your business.

04:41.990 --> 04:42.820
Why, you!

04:51.570 --> 04:51.970
Thank...

04:53.300 --> 04:54.910
What are you doing?!

04:54.910 --> 04:57.240
Stop flitting about, tulip head.

04:57.240 --> 04:58.440
Tu, tu...

04:58.440 --> 05:00.310
Who are you calling a tulip head?!

05:00.310 --> 05:01.950
Who else other than you?

05:01.950 --> 05:04.320
How rude! Of all people, you've got some nerve to...

05:04.320 --> 05:05.620
I got it!

05:05.620 --> 05:07.290
Hayate, I'm going to do it!

05:07.290 --> 05:09.250
Now, let's get ready!

05:09.250 --> 05:15.120
Hey! Listen until they're finished when people are talking to you!

05:23.200 --> 05:24.400
Not done yet, Kei?

05:24.400 --> 05:25.770
Hurry, hurry!

05:25.770 --> 05:28.010
Be quiet. Don't rush me.

05:28.010 --> 05:31.410
Can you really tell where the demon larvae will appear?

05:31.410 --> 05:36.120
I'm inputting the data from the previous demon larvae to predict the next seed's location.

05:37.050 --> 05:37.980
There it is.

05:41.250 --> 05:42.910
That place is...

05:43.420 --> 05:44.620
The Awayuki residence.

05:44.620 --> 05:47.560
That's where Himeno lives, isn't it?

05:48.090 --> 05:50.060
This is getting interesting!

05:50.060 --> 05:52.760
All right! Let's go report this to Himeno!

05:56.630 --> 06:02.560
Appearance Probability

05:57.200 --> 06:02.560
Demon Larvae Prediction Program

05:59.100 --> 06:02.560
An appearance probability of twenty-five percent?

06:05.510 --> 06:07.170
There's no need for me to go then.

06:07.650 --> 06:10.050
A demon larva seed somewhere in the Awayuki residence?!

06:10.050 --> 06:12.920
Yeah, though we don't know its exact location.

06:12.920 --> 06:16.290
Let's find the demon larva seed ourselves and exterminate it!

06:16.290 --> 06:18.050
With these members?!

06:19.060 --> 06:21.890
But don't you think we need to prepare a little more?

06:21.890 --> 06:24.000
You don't want to go?

06:24.000 --> 06:24.660
That's not...

06:24.660 --> 06:27.320
Well, then you don't have to. We'll go find it ourselves.

06:29.170 --> 06:32.470
So you have to look after them well...

06:35.010 --> 06:37.610
...and protect them.

06:37.610 --> 06:38.800
Mom...

06:40.950 --> 06:42.010
All right!

06:42.010 --> 06:43.750
I understand! I'll go too!

06:43.750 --> 06:44.780
All right!

06:44.780 --> 06:48.720
In return, listen to what I say and don't do anything dangerous.

06:49.090 --> 06:50.690
I'm not a kid!

06:50.690 --> 06:52.750
At any rate, just leave it to me!

06:54.760 --> 06:57.700
All right! We'll start looking in this forest.

06:57.700 --> 07:00.260
Everyone, follow my lead!

07:04.440 --> 07:08.210
She didn't grow up in this house?

07:08.210 --> 07:13.140
Yeah, her real mother passed away when she was very young.

07:13.140 --> 07:16.410
She's probably been lonely all this time.

07:16.950 --> 07:19.220
Hayate, you're a friend of hers, aren't you?

07:19.220 --> 07:21.920
Well, it's not really like that.

07:21.920 --> 07:26.120
At any rate, please get along with her.

07:30.700 --> 07:33.000
What is this, anyway?!

07:33.000 --> 07:35.230
It's probably a trap someone set.

07:35.230 --> 07:36.000
Yeah...

07:36.000 --> 07:37.560
Poor Himeno.

07:38.000 --> 07:40.800
Whatever, just get me down!

07:41.610 --> 07:44.170
Are you all right, Himeno?

07:46.510 --> 07:49.710
Just who set this trap?

07:49.710 --> 07:50.870
That would be me.

07:51.620 --> 07:53.480
Mr. Tanaka?!

07:53.480 --> 07:58.980
For security reasons, there are various traps laid out all over the Awayuki family grounds!

07:59.460 --> 08:02.160
Then this is no place to be looking for a demon larva.

08:02.160 --> 08:03.130
A demon larva?

08:04.460 --> 08:09.100
Well, a demon larva is like an insect but sort of isn't...

08:09.100 --> 08:10.830
Please leave it to me!

08:11.900 --> 08:16.410
I may not look it, but I was called, Fabre Tanaka during my childhood!

08:16.410 --> 08:20.310
There wasn't a single person who was a match for me when it came to collecting insects.

08:20.310 --> 08:21.010
What?

08:21.880 --> 08:24.250
At any rate, let's start looking in the mansion!

08:27.190 --> 08:30.190
Miss, please wait! I will accompany you!

08:30.190 --> 08:31.710
Do wait, please!

08:42.530 --> 08:45.430
Himeno's
Garden

08:54.450 --> 08:55.910
What's with this?

08:56.410 --> 08:58.380
I feel like I'm getting lost in my own home.

09:01.690 --> 09:04.060
Come on, Himeno!

09:04.060 --> 09:05.750
Just a few more steps...

09:06.290 --> 09:09.190
Himeno, Himeno, Himeno, I'll put you in your place!

09:09.190 --> 09:13.720
You'll regret having dumped water on me with your low status!

09:13.800 --> 09:14.130
Man Who Gives Money to Charity

09:16.000 --> 09:18.060
Now!

09:21.710 --> 09:24.500
Leave insect hunting to Fabre Tanaka!

09:25.910 --> 09:27.310
What the?!

09:33.580 --> 09:35.350
This is honey.

09:35.350 --> 09:38.790
Perfect! Various types of beetles will be attracted.

09:38.790 --> 09:41.990
Why?

09:38.790 --> 09:41.990
Plus, this is of the highest quality, fitting of the Awayuki family.

09:41.990 --> 09:44.460
More importantly, why did honey...

09:47.270 --> 09:49.600
If only Tanaka hadn't shown up!

09:49.600 --> 09:51.100
Just you wait, Himeno!

09:51.100 --> 09:54.630
This time, I'll take this industrial-sized package of mayonnaise...

09:57.810 --> 09:59.480
That guy was Hayate!

09:59.480 --> 10:03.810
That slow-wit who doesn't understand my beauty is poking around!

10:08.450 --> 10:11.050
Hold it right there!

10:21.300 --> 10:22.500
Hey, you!

10:22.500 --> 10:23.690
Watch where you're...

10:24.600 --> 10:26.400
Are you all right?

10:26.800 --> 10:29.040
Oh, my, what a good-looking man.

10:29.040 --> 10:31.210
You seem to be all right. Excuse me.

10:31.210 --> 10:32.470
I'm in a hurry, so...

10:35.010 --> 10:37.620
You dump an industrial-sized package of mayonnaise on a lady...

10:37.620 --> 10:39.780
...and think it can be settled just by saying, "Are you all right?"

10:39.780 --> 10:40.790
Come with me!

10:40.790 --> 10:42.410
But I have a delivery to make!

10:42.920 --> 10:44.220
No need to be concerned about that!

10:46.590 --> 10:49.590
I see, your name is Go.

10:49.590 --> 10:50.960
Well...

10:53.500 --> 10:55.300
Be grateful to me.

10:55.300 --> 10:57.800
I'm going to especially forgive you for that offense so heinous...

10:57.800 --> 11:00.600
...that punishment by death would normally bring no complaints.

11:04.040 --> 11:06.770
Now Go will fall head over heels in love with me.

11:07.280 --> 11:13.050
It's a little daring, but for a naive man like him, this is an effective plan.

11:13.050 --> 11:14.850
Hey, Go! Give me a massa...

11:15.590 --> 11:16.590
Hello!

11:16.590 --> 11:19.190
Miss Takato! Why are you here?!

11:19.190 --> 11:24.360
I heard your mother and Mr. Tanaka were classmates, and I wanted some more details about that!

11:24.360 --> 11:26.800
What? I wouldn't know of such a thing.

11:26.800 --> 11:28.030
Anyway, where's Go?

11:28.030 --> 11:29.900
Go! That's right, a man needs to go for it!

11:29.900 --> 11:32.000
Knowing that it was a sin, she was drawn to a man...

11:32.000 --> 11:34.410
...who had a wife and children and agonized over the forbidden love!

11:34.410 --> 11:37.980
While aware of this, there was nothing Mr. Tanaka could have done!

11:37.980 --> 11:40.180
The classical literature class was like a torture chamber from Hell!

11:40.180 --> 11:42.980
He could only watch over those two who had eyes only for each other!

11:42.980 --> 11:45.450
Oh, Mr. Tanaka! How sentimental it is!

11:46.180 --> 11:48.290
What's with this girl?

11:48.290 --> 11:49.650
Tanaka!

11:50.150 --> 11:53.290
When it comes to insects, leave it to Fabre Tanaka!

11:53.290 --> 11:59.100
Around here, there are a lot of butterflies and the Masaki Uranamijano Butterflies are recommended.

11:59.100 --> 12:01.200
Why does it have that kind of a name?

12:01.200 --> 12:05.440
Because Dr. Masaki researched it.

12:02.500 --> 12:04.000
Hey, found a squirrel!

12:04.000 --> 12:05.440
Where? Where?

12:05.440 --> 12:09.210
Himeno, is it okay to have this old man around while searching for a demon larva?

12:09.210 --> 12:11.270
We couldn't lose him even if we tried!

12:11.840 --> 12:15.680
But it's weird. I don't sense the presence of a demon larva at all.

12:15.680 --> 12:17.680
That's because it's still a seed, isn't it?

12:17.680 --> 12:18.580
Even you couldn't detect...

12:18.580 --> 12:22.490
So, that insect is in some kind of seed!

12:22.490 --> 12:23.990
That is rather unusual!

12:23.990 --> 12:26.550
Mr. Tanaka! Drive! Drive!

12:27.790 --> 12:30.900
There is no need to worry. I have a driving history of fifteen years.

12:30.900 --> 12:34.850
I've been strolling and rolling along every day and I can drive even with my eyes closed.

12:35.500 --> 12:37.800
But your feet! How is this car running?!

12:38.640 --> 12:42.410
Well, that's because we're intensely rolling downhill!

12:42.410 --> 12:43.810
More like falling!

12:49.880 --> 12:54.440
This yard is perfect for searching out new species of insects!

12:55.690 --> 12:56.950
This is a yard?!

13:00.460 --> 13:03.220
I'm hearing some strange voices.

13:04.300 --> 13:08.030
The members of the Awayuki family love animals,

13:08.030 --> 13:10.560
...so we're raising many types of them here in captivity.

13:11.440 --> 13:13.100
Seems like a very dangerous place.

13:13.910 --> 13:16.400
I have to be strong and protect these kids!

13:16.970 --> 13:19.340
Okay, whatever you do, don't stray from me.

13:25.180 --> 13:28.250
That's right, they're in captivity, so they're pets.

13:28.250 --> 13:29.250
There's no way a large...

13:29.250 --> 13:31.060
Whoa! It's huge!

13:31.060 --> 13:32.660
Mr. Gorilla! Mr. Gorilla!

13:32.660 --> 13:34.330
Oh, hi, Michael.

13:34.330 --> 13:35.490
Michael?!

13:36.390 --> 13:38.590
Mannen! Hajime! Shin!

13:39.200 --> 13:40.490
Come ba...

13:41.000 --> 13:42.360
Hi, Rodriguez!

13:44.000 --> 13:46.200
Oh, don't worry, it's just playful biting.

13:51.910 --> 13:52.410
Special Coverage
Sasame's Words Gate

13:51.910 --> 13:52.410
What is the true identity
of the personality who
draws the girls
to him?

13:51.910 --> 13:52.410
Why are young girls
drawn to the radio?

13:52.410 --> 13:54.610
Thank you for the postcards, always.

13:55.250 --> 13:56.510
One more time...

14:00.080 --> 14:03.790
I'm sorry. I got lost.

14:03.790 --> 14:06.260
Which way to the plaster studio?

14:06.990 --> 14:08.790
The plaster studio is over there.

14:08.790 --> 14:10.590
Oh, thank you.

14:13.530 --> 14:14.690
How stupid.

14:22.140 --> 14:25.880
So that was connected all the way over here?

14:25.880 --> 14:27.980
That was a lot of fun!

14:27.980 --> 14:30.250
Mr. Gorilla even gave us a gift.

14:30.250 --> 14:32.580
Guys, this is not the time for that!

14:32.580 --> 14:34.740
We lost track of Himeno.

14:40.490 --> 14:43.490
Dummy! If you make a lot of noise, someone will come here!

14:43.490 --> 14:45.090
What's the matter, boys?

14:45.700 --> 14:47.900
My, you dropped your banana?

14:47.900 --> 14:50.100
Then, in exchange I'll give you these cookies.

14:50.100 --> 14:51.340
Where are you boys from?

14:51.340 --> 14:52.390
Leafenia's...

14:55.370 --> 14:56.970
We're going home now.

14:56.970 --> 14:58.880
Bye, Miss Maid!

14:58.880 --> 15:00.080
Bye!

15:00.080 --> 15:01.740
Be careful on your way back.

15:03.280 --> 15:05.150
Damn it, you talk too much.

15:05.150 --> 15:06.950
What a nice lady.

15:06.950 --> 15:10.250
In any case, we'd better look for Himeno.

15:10.250 --> 15:11.280
She's probably lost.

15:11.790 --> 15:12.950
Mannen!

15:13.890 --> 15:15.690
Hajime! Shin!

15:15.660 --> 15:18.830
Oh, it's all right. They're with Michael.

15:15.930 --> 15:17.800
Answer me!

15:18.830 --> 15:23.000
We should look for this new demon larva insect or whatever.

15:21.300 --> 15:23.000
I couldn't even protect those kids.

15:23.000 --> 15:25.900
I'm a failure as Prétear.

15:25.100 --> 15:26.640
Oh! It's you, Bob!

15:26.640 --> 15:27.410
Bob?

15:27.410 --> 15:29.110
Long time no see!

15:29.110 --> 15:30.330
Give me a hug!

15:31.240 --> 15:33.380
Hi, Roberto. Doing well?

15:33.380 --> 15:35.940
Juliet, you've grown so much.

15:36.750 --> 15:38.780
Claude, Claude, Claude!

15:37.280 --> 15:38.780
You don't need to say hello!

15:38.780 --> 15:40.790
Oh, Miss, please wait, wait, wait!

15:40.790 --> 15:42.750
Give it a rest already, Mr. Tanaka!

15:43.490 --> 15:46.990
This swamp area has a lot of marshy grounds, so watch your step.

15:46.990 --> 15:48.980
So tell me before I fall in!

15:49.530 --> 15:52.590
I have to find those kids or else they'll be in danger.

15:54.130 --> 15:56.230
Something's pulling on my leg!

15:56.230 --> 15:58.800
Oh, that's probably Pierre.

15:58.800 --> 15:59.790
Pierre?!

16:00.340 --> 16:02.400
What is Pierre?!

16:04.640 --> 16:05.980
Hang on, everyone.

16:05.980 --> 16:08.180
I'll come save you all.

16:08.180 --> 16:11.850
We sure can't find this new demon larva insect.

16:11.850 --> 16:14.320
But to discover a new species, patience is...

16:14.750 --> 16:15.990
Oh, hi, Marilyn.

16:15.990 --> 16:18.160
What? You found an unusual animal?!

16:18.160 --> 16:19.450
Well done, Marilyn!

16:20.090 --> 16:23.060
Mr. Tanaka?! Where are you going?!

16:23.890 --> 16:24.880
He's gone...

16:30.070 --> 16:31.900
What?!

16:37.170 --> 16:39.010
Found you, Himeno!

16:40.880 --> 16:41.940
Himeno?

16:42.580 --> 16:44.050
Sorry to have kept you waiting!

16:44.050 --> 16:47.890
This, this! The South Pole style curry from Bistro Blanche!

16:47.890 --> 16:49.320
It's good!

16:49.320 --> 16:52.890
Sorry for being late. I was grabbed by some strange person.

16:52.890 --> 16:55.550
How dangerous. Here, Hayate, let's eat.

16:56.990 --> 16:58.960
What are you doing, Hayate?

16:59.700 --> 17:00.800
I'm working.

17:00.800 --> 17:01.860
I see.

17:02.500 --> 17:03.300
Well then, thanks!

17:03.300 --> 17:04.960
Thanks for the delivery!

17:11.480 --> 17:13.080
I'm exhausted.

17:13.080 --> 17:15.080
We didn't find a demon larva after all.

17:15.080 --> 17:17.640
Well, it's good that we didn't find one.

17:18.620 --> 17:20.240
There's a lot of flowers.

17:20.720 --> 17:23.720
What? There's one that's different.

17:23.720 --> 17:26.890
I raised that one with my mom.

17:26.890 --> 17:28.360
It's my treasure.

17:35.000 --> 17:35.590
Shin!

17:42.670 --> 17:44.200
Don't touch the flowers!

17:51.180 --> 17:52.050
Mannen!

17:54.950 --> 17:55.490
Hayate?

17:55.490 --> 17:56.650
Don't get distracted!

17:58.290 --> 17:59.590
Himeno!

18:38.130 --> 18:39.360
<i>Beyondios!</i>

18:49.440 --> 18:50.700
Himeno, now!

18:51.480 --> 18:52.240
Got it!

18:53.280 --> 18:54.740
Water Flail!

19:04.590 --> 19:05.890
We did it, Himeno!

19:06.420 --> 19:07.830
Are you hurt, Hajime?

19:07.830 --> 19:09.590
Not really.

19:09.590 --> 19:11.230
Mannen? Shin?

19:11.230 --> 19:12.530
Nothing.

19:12.530 --> 19:14.230
I'm okay.

19:14.230 --> 19:15.730
Thank goodness...

19:15.730 --> 19:17.530
What? What's the matter?

19:17.530 --> 19:18.590
I'm sorry!

19:19.070 --> 19:20.470
What the...

19:20.470 --> 19:21.530
I...

19:23.270 --> 19:25.180
If I had been more responsible...

19:25.180 --> 19:25.940
Himeno...

19:29.580 --> 19:32.240
The flowers are saying, "Thank you."

19:36.090 --> 19:37.250
Mom...

19:38.590 --> 19:41.190
It's great that we were able to protect the flowers.

19:41.190 --> 19:44.030
Too bad I didn't get a chance to be the hero though.

19:44.030 --> 19:46.760
You were saved by Himeno!

19:46.760 --> 19:48.030
Why, you!

19:48.030 --> 19:48.830
Hayate!

19:48.830 --> 19:51.530
Your father's calling you, tulip head.

19:56.440 --> 19:58.140
What is it, Dad?

19:58.140 --> 19:59.380
Ta-daa!

19:59.380 --> 20:03.680
I finished my latest piece! I wanted you to be the first to see it!

20:03.680 --> 20:05.150
Pull the string, pull!

20:05.780 --> 20:07.220
Ta-ta-da!

20:06.920 --> 20:07.580
Himeno

20:07.220 --> 20:09.550
It's titled, "Himeno!"

20:13.790 --> 20:17.430
How terrible, Himeno! It was such a nice piece!

20:17.430 --> 20:18.260
No, it wasn't!

20:18.600 --> 20:19.830
Oh, fantastic!

20:19.830 --> 20:21.700
Mr. Tanaka, it must have been tough for you...

20:21.700 --> 20:24.370
...to have seen her agonize over the forbidden love with her teacher!

20:24.370 --> 20:28.040
To think, you got so jealous, you hit him and got expelled!

20:28.040 --> 20:31.240
<i>Then that teacher was transferred to Paris,</i>

20:28.040 --> 20:31.240
This is the unusual animal you located?

20:31.240 --> 20:34.680
<i>...she followed him by plane and you rushed in your car after her,</i>

20:34.680 --> 20:37.980
<i>...got into a car accident, and lost your memories!</i>

20:43.590 --> 20:48.420
To think you'd go to the trouble of working under her father in order to watch over her.

20:49.190 --> 20:50.160
I...

20:51.030 --> 20:55.230
I'm going to fulfill my mission as a Leafe Knight in my own way.

20:56.870 --> 20:59.230
A Knight's mission?

21:01.170 --> 21:06.300
<i>There are feelings you want to communicate, but can't get yourself to do so, right?</i>

21:07.080 --> 21:11.180
<i>It's very important to you, but you do the opposite and push away.</i>

21:11.180 --> 21:14.640
<i>You want to be near a person, but it takes all of your effort to just watch from a distance.</i>

21:15.490 --> 21:18.490
<i>However, your feelings will surely get through.</i>

21:18.490 --> 21:19.960
<i>Someday, surely...</i>

21:23.300 --> 21:29.000
Staring out the window of a room with the lights off

21:23.300 --> 21:29.000
akari o keshita heya no mado kara miru

21:29.000 --> 21:33.240
The stars shine in the night sky

21:29.000 --> 21:33.240
yozora ni hoshi ga hikaru

21:33.240 --> 21:39.110
Today will definitely be a search for your constellation

21:33.240 --> 21:39.110
kyo koso anata no seiza sagashi

21:39.110 --> 21:41.980
To give you an arbitrary jinx

21:39.110 --> 21:41.980
katte na jinkusu

21:41.980 --> 21:47.960
If you find the seventh star, then it's the Lucky Star

21:41.980 --> 21:47.960
nanatsume no hoshi o mitsuketara <i>Lucky</i> <i>Star</i>

21:47.960 --> 21:51.930
Tomorrow, with a happy face

21:47.960 --> 21:51.930
ashita wa egao de

21:51.930 --> 21:58.030
I'll greet you good morning

21:51.930 --> 21:58.030
ohayoutte koe o kakete ageru wa

21:58.030 --> 22:02.340
It's a special thing you can't do anything about

21:58.030 --> 22:02.340
shikatanai tokubetsu

22:02.340 --> 22:03.700
My Sweet Heart

22:02.340 --> 22:03.700
My Sweet Heart

22:03.700 --> 22:10.010
I can't be the only one engrossed in all of this

22:03.700 --> 22:10.010
watashi bakari ga muchuu da nante masaka

22:10.010 --> 22:13.780
It just can't be, and I won't stand for it

22:10.010 --> 22:13.780
arienai yurusenai

22:13.780 --> 22:20.790
I want to see what you're feeling in your heart

22:13.780 --> 22:20.790
anata no naka no kimochi nozokitai

22:20.790 --> 22:29.130
To do it secretly, without you knowing

22:20.790 --> 22:29.130
kizukarenai you ni naisho de

22:41.670 --> 22:43.640
Mannen, what exactly is the Princess of Disaster?

22:43.640 --> 22:46.580
When you're troubled, just prét with me!

22:46.580 --> 22:47.540
Really?

22:47.640 --> 22:50.540
Smile of Darkness

22:47.980 --> 22:50.540
Then, I won't be beaten in the next episode either!
